    "text": "<p>A thermodynamic system is taken from an original state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> to an intermediate state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> by the linear process shown in the figure. Its volume is then reduced to the original volume from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> by an isobaric process. The total work done by the gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6e88af83-8b52-4a85-9bef-1f8089e65a6e-image.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 195px;\" /></p>",
